><td align="left">39.04</td><td align="left">38.39</td><td align="left">39.69</td><td align="left">10.1</td><td></td></tr><tr><td align="left">2</td><td align="left">39.70</td><td align="left">38.85</td><td align="left">40.55</td><td align="left">11.2</td><td></td></tr><tr><td align="left">3</td><td align="left">40.41</td><td align="left">39.55</td><td align="left">41.27</td><td align="left">11.5</td><td></td></tr><tr><td align="left">4</td><td align="left">39.45</td><td align="left">38.51</td><td align="left">40.40</td><td align="left">10.3</td><td></td></tr><tr><td align="left">5+</td><td align="left">39.99</td><td align="left">39.12</td><td align="left">40.87</td><td align="left">9.3</td><td></td></tr><tr><td colspan="6"><hr></hr></td></tr><tr><td align="left">Age</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td align="left">0.10</td></tr><tr><td align="left">-19</td><td align="left">40.25</td><td align="left">39.16</td><td align="left">41.35</td><td align="left">12.3</td><td></td></tr><tr><td align="left">20&#x02013;24</td><td align="left">39.98</td><td align="left">39.37</td><td align="left">40.58</td><td align="left">10.4</td><td></td></tr><tr><td align="left">25&#x02013;29</td><td align="left">39.53</td><td align="left">39.01</td><td align="left">40.06</td><td align="left">10.0</td><td></td></tr><tr><td align="left">30&#x02013;34</td><td align="left">38.55</td><td align="left">37.81</td><td align="left">39.28</td><td align="left">11.9</td><td></td></tr><tr><td align="left">35+</td><td align="left">39.41</td><td align="left">38.28</td><td align="left">40.55</td><td align="left">9.7</td><td></td></tr></tbody></table></table-wrap><table-wrap position="float" id="T9"><label>Table 9</label><caption><p>Effects of maternal ethnicity, weight, height, body mass index (BMI), parity, and age on head circumference (HC)</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr><td align="left">Maternal factor</td><td align="left">Mean</td><td align="left">95%CI</td><td></td